From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: Add Orange Pi 5 MIPI LCD overlays

The Orange Pi 5 has two 4-lane MIPI DSI LCD connectors, named LCD1 and
LCD2 in the Orange Pi 5 user manual (section 3.31). The Orange Pi BSP
device trees wire LCD1 to DSI0/MIPI DCPHY0 and LCD2 to DSI1/MIPI
DCPHY1, each with its own LCD power enable GPIO, panel reset GPIO,
backlight PWM and touch I2C bus:

         power en  reset     backlight     touch I2C   touch INT/RESET
  LCD1   GPIO1_A0  GPIO1_B1  PWM2_M0       I2C7_M0     GPIO1_B5/GPIO1_B4
  LCD2   GPIO1_A1  GPIO1_B3  PWM6_M0       I2C2_M0     GPIO1_A7/GPIO1_A4

Source: rk3588s-orangepi.dtsi, rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi and
rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd.dtsi in
https://github.com/orangepi-xunlong/linux-orangepi, branch
orange-pi-6.1-rk35xx.

Add one overlay per connector for the official Orange Pi 10.1" MIPI
LCD (Innolux AFJ101-BA2131 with a Goodix GT9271 touch controller), so
that boards without a panel are unaffected. LCD1 is fed from VP3, the
same VOP2 to DSI0 routing other mainline RK3588 boards use; LCD2 is fed
from VP2 so that both connectors can be used at the same time. VP0
(HDMI0) and VP1 stay free.

Also add overlay application tests. They make kbuild build
rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtb and rk3588s-orangepi-5-sata.dtb with -@, so
that the overlays can be applied to them by the boot loader.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile         |  14 ++
 .../dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd1.dtso | 131 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd2.dtso | 130 +++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 275 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd1.dtso
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd2.dtso

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
index 96bcfde1cef1..95454a66366b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
@@ -233,6 +233,8 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-nanopi-r6s.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-nanopi-r6c.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-odroid-m2.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd1.dtbo
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd2.dtbo
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5-sata.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5b.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5-pro.dtb
@@ -344,3 +346,15 @@ rk3588-rock-5b-plus-radxa-4k-cam-dtbs := rk3588-rock-5b-plus.dtb \
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588-tiger-haikou-haikou-video-demo.dtb
 rk3588-tiger-haikou-haikou-video-demo-dtbs := rk3588-tiger-haikou.dtb \
 	rk3588-tiger-haikou-video-demo.dtbo
+
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588s-orangepi-5-lcd1.dtb
